From 0418a0d98343c87d1a8aa86acb1ad3f2a1ed3b5e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stacho_P <stacho@venco.com.pl>
Date: Mon, 6 Jul 2026 19:54:40 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] qualcommax: archer-ax55-v1: LAN works - 2.5G HSGMII trunk
 passes traffic

The RTL8367S<->IPQ5018 trunk (SGMII 1G and HSGMII 2.5G) now passes
traffic from a cold boot. Two rtl8365mb driver pieces were missing,
and BOTH are required - each alone leaves a link-up trunk that drops
every frame in both directions:

1. Disable SGMII in-band autoneg in the SerDes (SDS reg 0x0002 bit 9,
   bit 8 = commit; vendor rtl8367c_setSgmiiNway, 8051 paused around
   the access). The SerDes powers up with AN enabled; on a fixed-link
   trunk the handshake never completes and the SerDes silently drops
   all frames while the forced link still reports up.

2. Force link/speed/duplex/pause in SDS_MISC (0x1D11) from
   mac_link_up, as vendor setAsicPortForceLinkExt does for ext id 1.
   Bit 9 (link force) directly gates the SerDes TX.

Also:
- ship the TP-Link GPL 1223-byte Sgmii_Init 8051 firmware (PKG_RELEASE 2)
- WiFi BDFs for TP-LINK-AX55-V1 calibration variant (ipq-wifi)
- ax55-testdefaults v3: WiFi config moved to ieee80211 hotplug (ath11k
  registers PHYs after uci-defaults run)
- DTS: switch reset GPIO 33, switch child mdio node with PHYs 0-3,
  trunk at 2500base-x (validated against the stock DTB: golden config
  runs the trunk at 1G, 2.5G works with this driver)
- 0919: regmap-debugfs writes enabled (bring-up aid, drop for upstream)

Debugging details: SDS status reg 0x3D (SigDet/Sync/Link), never dump
the full switch regmap over MDIO (wedges the MDIO slave until power
cycle), the switch 8051 polls INDACS continuously so pause it (0x130C
bit 5) around any INDACS access from the host.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
